#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Archive Supabase rows to R2 before they leave the database.

Rule of the project: nothing collected is discarded. Rows are written to the
private backups bucket (gzip JSONL plus a manifest), downloaded back and
checked (sha256 and row count), and only then cleared or deleted in the
database, in one statement that locks the rows of the day and acts only if
they still match the manifest.

Tables (one object per day, America/Sao_Paulo):
  consultas            after 7 days, clear api_response (the copy of
                       placa_cache.payload that nothing reads). Only rows the
                       leads extraction already read (its watermark) and only
                       while no INSERT policy is open on consultas (A16).
  api_chamadas         after 30 days, summarize the day (api_chamadas_resumir)
                       and delete the raw rows, except the paid sources wdapi
                       and placafipe that the fin reads.
  eventos_funil        after 30 days, summarize the day (eventos_funil_resumir:
                       eventos_funil_diario and funil_diario_arquivo) and
                       delete the raw rows.
  relatorio_aberturas  after 180 days, delete the raw rows (replaces the
                       pg_cron job that deleted them without an archive).
  placa_cache          "podar": archive, then delete the cache rows past their
                       use: not found and older than 6 hours, and found but
                       older than 90 days, except plates with a paid order.

Usage:
  pc-supabase-arquivar <tabela> arquivar --dia 2026-08-03
  pc-supabase-arquivar <tabela> arquivar --de 2026-08-03 --ate 2026-11-19 [--pausa 10]
  pc-supabase-arquivar <tabela> liberar --ate 2026-11-11 [--vacuum-a-cada 10] [--confirmar]
  pc-supabase-arquivar <tabela> diario [--confirmar]
  pc-supabase-arquivar <tabela> status
  pc-supabase-arquivar placa_cache podar [--limite 5000] [--confirmar]

"liberar" clears the column (consultas) or deletes (the others); "zerar" is
kept as its alias. "diario" archives every closed day missing since the last
archived one, then releases the days past the retention. Options: --ref
<project ref> (default prod), --prefixo <R2 prefix>. Without --confirmar,
liberar, diario and podar only print what they would do. --vacuum-a-cada N
runs a plain VACUUM after every N released days and at the end.
"""
